<section class="make" id="making">
  <div class="make-img" style="background-image:url(https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0798/8602/4945/files/em-55e980b842013b51.jpg)"><span class="make-tag">Honey travertine · one block</span></div>
  <div class="make-body">
    <p class="make-k rv">03 — The making</p>
    <h2 class="make-h rv d1">Carved from one block.<br>No seams. No shortcuts.</h2>
    <p class="make-p rv d2">Every vessel begins as a single quarried block, cut and carved until the grain itself decides where the water gathers. Because the piece is one continuous run of stone, the veining is unbroken — and no two are ever alike. The interior is brought to a mirror; the exterior is left at the finish the stone calls for.</p>
    <p class="make-p rv d3">Walls are carved to a 60&nbsp;mm standard and labelled to the exact millimetre on the production drawings you approve. Nothing leaves until it has passed its water test, and every commission travels with its measured weights and a chain-of-custody document, from quarry to door.</p>
    <p class="make-note rv d4">Every commission travels under transit insurance, the sum insured stated in writing on your order.<br>We ship worldwide; within the US, delivered duty-paid to your threshold — nothing payable on arrival.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band"><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0798/8602/4945/files/em-65f75c909cd04669.jpg" alt="" data-para="55"><div class="band-scrim"></div><div class="band-txt"><p class="band-line rv">Warm as the desert it came from.</p><p class="band-sub rv d1">Dune · Golden Sandstone</p></div></section>

<section class="curated" id="service">
  <div class="curated-lede">
    <p class="curated-k rv">04 — Clientele &amp; service</p>
    <h2 class="curated-h rv d1">For the home that is built once.</h2>
    <p class="curated-p rv d2">Atelier Earthmade is not a catalogue. Each vessel is commissioned for a single room — for the architects, collectors and owners making a house they intend to keep. One conversation, one block of stone, one piece that will outlast the room around it.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="curated-cols">
    <div class="cpill rv"><p class="cpill-k">Privately curated</p><h3 class="cpill-t">A craftsman, not a sales desk</h3><p class="cpill-d">You are matched with an account manager who knows the stone. Material, dimensions and finish are chosen for your room alone — one vessel, carved for one home.</p></div>
    <div class="cpill rv d1"><p class="cpill-k">Worldwide · duty-paid in the US</p><h3 class="cpill-t">Delivered, insured, to your threshold</h3><p class="cpill-d">We ship worldwide. Within the United States the price is all-inclusive: ocean freight, export crating, transit insurance and every import duty settled before the piece ships, delivered by appointment to your ground-floor threshold — nothing to pay on arrival. Outside the US, freight and duty are arranged and quoted for your country.</p></div>
    <div class="cpill rv d2"><p class="cpill-k">Kept for a lifetime</p><h3 class="cpill-t">An object to be inherited</h3><p class="cpill-d">Stone does not date. Each vessel arrives with its measured weights, a care guide and a chain-of-custody document — the beginning of a piece that will be passed on, not replaced.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="terms">
    <div class="term rv"><p class="term-k">The 72-hour window</p><p class="term-d">When you place an order we hold your piece and <b>process the transaction, then confirm every detail with you by email within 72 hours</b> — access, floor loading and the delivery route for your address. Inside that window either of us may cancel, for any reason, with a full refund. Only once it closes is the block bought and cut, and the commission becomes final.</p></div>
    <div class="term rv d1"><p class="term-k">Transit insurance</p><p class="term-d">Every vessel travels fully insured in transit, with the <b>sum insured stated in writing on your order</b>. The cover runs from the workshop to your threshold, carried in the price — there is nothing for you to arrange.</p></div>
    <div class="term rv d2"><p class="term-k">If it arrives damaged</p><p class="term-d">Inspect the crate on delivery. If the piece is damaged, <b>refuse the delivery and do not sign for it</b> — that refusal is precisely what allows the insurance claim to proceed. We then remake the piece or refund you in full. A signed acceptance closes that door, so please look first.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

