<section class="timeline" id="timeline">
  <div class="tl-hd">
    <p class="tl-k rv">The commission</p>
    <h2 class="tl-h rv d1">From first message to your threshold.</h2>
    <p class="tl-sub rv d2">One dedicated account manager, the whole way through — no queue, no hand-offs. Here is exactly how it goes.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="tl-steps">
    <div class="tl-step rv"><span class="tl-n">01</span><p class="tl-when">Within 24 hours</p><h3 class="tl-t">A person, not a queue</h3><p class="tl-d">You are matched with a dedicated account manager who knows the stone — the same person from first message to delivery. We reply within 24 hours, every time.</p></div>
    <div class="tl-step rv d1"><span class="tl-n">02</span><p class="tl-when">The 72-hour window</p><h3 class="tl-t">Choose your stone</h3><p class="tl-d">We send you photographs of the actual blocks and guide you through material, finish and dimensions for your room. The transaction is processed and confirmed by email — and either of us may cancel for a full refund until the window closes.</p></div>
    <div class="tl-step rv d2"><span class="tl-n">03</span><p class="tl-when">14–22 weeks</p><h3 class="tl-t">Carved, and kept in view</h3><p class="tl-d">Your block is cut and carved by hand. Your manager follows up with photographs at each phase — rough, refined, then the polished interior — so you watch it become yours.</p></div>
    <div class="tl-step rv"><span class="tl-n">04</span><p class="tl-when">Before it ships</p><h3 class="tl-t">Water-tested &amp; crated</h3><p class="tl-d">Every piece is water-tested, then crated and fully insured. We settle the freight and all US import duty as the importer of record.</p></div>
    <div class="tl-step rv d1"><span class="tl-n">05</span><p class="tl-when">To your door</p><h3 class="tl-t">Delivered worldwide</h3><p class="tl-d">Delivered to your threshold by our white-glove partners — freight, duty and insurance carried in the price. Full placement, and a ceremonial unboxing, on request — so it feels like opening something rare.</p></div>
    <div class="tl-step rv d2"><span class="tl-n">06</span><p class="tl-when">For a lifetime</p><h3 class="tl-t">Cared for, after</h3><p class="tl-d">Your vessel arrives with its measured weights, a care guide and a chain-of-custody document. Your manager stays reachable for the life of the piece.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="deliv" id="delivery">
  <div class="deliv-hd">
    <p class="deliv-k rv">White-glove delivery partnership</p>
    <h2 class="deliv-h rv d1">How a tonne of stone reaches your bathroom.</h2>
    <p class="deliv-sub rv d2">A vessel weighs from 300 to over 1,200&nbsp;kg. We move it with our white-glove logistics partners — specialists in monolithic stone. The freight, every duty and tariff, transit insurance and door-to-door delivery to your threshold are all carried in the price and choreographed to your building. Moving a tonne of stone is our craft, not your problem.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="deliv-grid">
    <div class="deliv-c rv"><p class="deliv-n">01</p><h3 class="deliv-t">Access &amp; load survey</h3><p class="deliv-d">Before a block is cut we confirm the route in writing — doorway widths, stair turns, lift dimensions and the floor's load rating. If the structure needs reinforcing beneath the piece, we tell you early, with the exact figures for your engineer.</p></div>
    <div class="deliv-c rv d1"><p class="deliv-n">02</p><h3 class="deliv-t">Custom crate &amp; sea freight</h3><p class="deliv-d">Each vessel is foamed, braced and sealed inside a bespoke timber crate built to its own weights, then shipped by sea on a dedicated pallet. Transit insurance runs from the workshop, the sum insured stated on your order.</p></div>
    <div class="deliv-c rv d2"><p class="deliv-n">03</p><h3 class="deliv-t">Rigging the last metres</h3><p class="deliv-d">The hardest part is the final room. Our crew moves the piece on stair-skates and machine dollies — or by crane and window-hoist where a staircase will not take it — planned to your building in advance, never improvised on the day.</p></div>
    <div class="deliv-c rv"><p class="deliv-n">04</p><h3 class="deliv-t">White-glove placement</h3><p class="deliv-d">On request, our white-glove partners uncrate, carry, set and level the vessel exactly where it will live, check the seal, and remove every scrap of packaging — the full hands-in-your-home service, so the first time you see it, it is simply there.</p></div>
    <div class="deliv-c rv d1"><p class="deliv-n">05</p><h3 class="deliv-t">Ready for your plumber</h3><p class="deliv-d">Vessels are freestanding; you choose floor- or wall-fed fillers and the waste position. We supply a drain-and-tap template and the exact rough-in drawings, so your plumber pre-sets everything before the piece arrives.</p></div>
    <div class="deliv-c rv d2"><p class="deliv-n">06</p><h3 class="deliv-t">If anything is wrong</h3><p class="deliv-d">Inspect the crate before you sign. If the piece is damaged you refuse delivery and do not sign — that refusal is precisely what lets us remake it or refund you in full. No argument, no chasing.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="faq-hd">
    <p class="faq-k rv">Questions, answered plainly</p>
    <h2 class="faq-h rv d1">The honest answers.</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="faq-list">
    <div class="faq-item rv"><h3 class="faq-q">Why does it cost this much?</h3><p class="faq-a">You are paying for one block of natural stone, carved by hand over months, then shipped fully insured and duty-paid to your door. The price is the piece, the ocean freight, every customs charge and the guarantee — all of it, settled before it ships. Nothing is added at the border. A cheaper listing is almost always a thinner stone, a resin cast, or a cost passed to you on arrival.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item rv"><h3 class="faq-q">How long will it last?</h3><p class="faq-a">Stone outlasts the house around it. Sealed and simply cared for, an Earthmade vessel is an heirloom — the kind of object that is inherited, not replaced. Each one ships with a care guide, and your manager stays reachable for its lifetime.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item rv"><h3 class="faq-q">What if it doesn't fit, or arrives damaged?</h3><p class="faq-a">We confirm your dimensions, floor loading and delivery access in writing before a single block is cut — nothing is left to chance. If a piece arrives damaged, you refuse the delivery and do not sign; that refusal is what lets us remake it or refund you in full.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item rv"><h3 class="faq-q">Can I see the actual stone first?</h3><p class="faq-a">Yes. During the 72-hour window your account manager sends photographs of the real blocks, so you choose the exact stone — veining and all — before anything is committed. It is the opposite of a stock photo.</p></div>
    <div class="faq-item rv"><h3 class="faq-q">Can I pay over time?</h3><p class="faq-a">Yes. At checkout you can pay in full or split the cost into monthly payments with Shop&nbsp;Pay Installments — the option appears automatically at the payment step when eligible. Everything is processed securely through Shopify; nothing is handled off-platform.</p></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="trade" id="trade">
  <div class="trade-in">
    <div class="trade-txt">
      <p class="trade-k rv">Trade &amp; hospitality</p>
      <h2 class="trade-h rv d1">For the people who specify.</h2>
      <p class="trade-p rv d2">Interior designers, architects, developers and hoteliers work with Atelier Earthmade on trade terms. One point of contact, technical drawings and CAD blocks for specification, physical stone samples for client presentations, and project pricing across multiple rooms or keys. Your client sees the vessel; you hold the relationship.</p>
      <ul class="trade-l rv d2">
        <li>Trade pricing &amp; project terms, quoted per specification</li>
        <li>CAD blocks, rough-in drawings and measured weights for your set</li>
        <li>Physical stone samples couriered for client presentations</li>
        <li>A dedicated trade account manager, from spec to installed</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="trade-cta rv d2">
      <button class="trade-b" onclick="openTrade()">Open a trade account →</button>
      <p class="trade-note">Designers · architects · developers · hospitality.<br>Trade &amp; press enquiries: trade@atelierearthmade.com</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

